## Self-Hosted Bot API Server — tdlib/telegram-bot-api

Source: github.com/tdlib/telegram-bot-api
License: BSL-1.0 (Boost)
Language: C++ (C++17)
Version: 10.2 (2026-07-14)

---

## What it is

The ACTUAL Bot API server that Telegram runs at api.telegram.org.
You can self-host it and get your own instance with lifted limits.
NOT a client library — it's the server itself.

## Why self-host

--local mode unlocks:
- File downloads: NO size limit (api.telegram.org caps at 20MB)
- File uploads: up to 2GB (vs 50MB)
- Local file path uploads via file:// URI (no HTTP upload needed)
- HTTP webhooks (not just HTTPS) — no SSL cert needed for dev
- Any local IP for webhooks (127.0.0.1, LAN, etc.)
- Webhook connections: up to 100,000 (vs 40 on public API)
- Direct file path responses (no download round-trip)

## Build

Dependencies: OpenSSL, zlib, gperf, CMake 3.10+
Compilers: Clang 5.0+ / GCC 7.0+ / MSVC 19.1+ / Intel 19+

```bash
git clone --recursive https://github.com/tdlib/telegram-bot-api.git
cd telegram-bot-api
mkdir build && cd build
cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release ..
cmake --build . --target install
```

## Run

```bash
telegram-bot-api --api-id=<ID> --api-hash=<HASH> --local
```

Required:
  --api-id=N          Telegram API ID (from my.telegram.org)
  --api-hash=STRING   Telegram API hash
  OR: TELEGRAM_API_ID / TELEGRAM_API_HASH env vars

Key options:
  --local             Enable local mode (lifted limits)
  --http-port=N       HTTP port (default 8081)
  --help              Full options list

